  <!-- ------------------------------------------------------------ grid -->
  <section class="pane" data-pane="grid" hidden>
    <div class="runner">
      <div class="runnerhead">
        <div>
          <strong>The same questions, asked as four different people.</strong>
          <p class="dim">
            Personalization is the part of the answer determined by who is asking rather
            than by what was asked. Hold the questions fixed, vary the person, and what
            changes is the whole of it. Two of these rows are not profiles:
            <em>no profile</em> is the baseline, and <em>Sam again</em> is the same
            request a second time — whatever differs there is the model disagreeing
            with itself, and it is the bar the other rows have to clear.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="runnerbuttons">
          <button id="runGrid" type="button">run the grid</button>
          <button id="stopGrid" type="button" hidden>stop</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="gridStatus" class="status"></div>
      <div id="gridOut" class="out"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- -------------------------------------------------------- ablation -->
  <section class="pane" data-pane="ablation" hidden>
    <div class="runner">
      <div class="runnerhead">
        <div>
          <strong>Which fields is it actually taking into account?</strong>
          <p class="dim">
            One profile, one field removed at a time, the same questions re-asked. A
            field whose removal changes nothing about the answer was never being taken
            into account — and it is paying for its tokens in the system block of every
            request, forever.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="runnerbuttons">
          <label class="dim">on
            <select id="ablationWho"></select>
          </label>
          <button id="runAblation" type="button">run the ablation</button>
          <button id="stopAblation" type="button" hidden>stop</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="ablationStatus" class="status"></div>
      <div id="ablationOut" class="out"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

